In article <2iqvtn$82a@gollum.dd.chalmers.se>, lundgren@dd.chalmers.se (Lars
Lundgren) says:
>
>Isn't there a bug involved here? Isn't it true that gelatinous cubes
>swallow everything, but only destroy 'soft' things (wood, leather,...)
>In one of my games, eating a bag caused _all_ the contents to disappear.

Your bag of holding is kinda like a gateway to some extra-dimensional
space.  That's why it can hold so much (though that doesn't explain
why it still has a weight... probably just a game limitation).
If the cube eats your bag, then you just can't get at the stuff anymore.

Putting the WoC into the BoH destroys this gate (and the bag explodes)
Putting a BoT or another BoH just blows up out of metaphysical illogic.
Unlike another poster, then, I don't believe that the gelatinous cube
should explode when it eats a BoH; it would just make the bag go away.
SImilary, since the BoT is like a BoH leading to a monster generator,
there wouldn't be any special effects (or new monsters) when this bag
gets eaten either.  That just leaves the ordinary sack, which oughta
leave behind things the cube won't eat.

Just my 2 Au on the subject.

